  Callerslog Cutter (CLC) is a small, fast and VERY powerfull tool which is
             able to keep your callerslog as small as you want!

  Aquarius/Outlaws released a kind of this door some months ago but his one
was slow (slower!) and sometimes fucked up some callerslog entrys by cutting
              them in pieces even if it should not (doc said!).

   CLC/SAD is the solution for all your LONG callerslog`s storing hundrets
                                  of calls.

 CLC is not working the way Aquarius do. We don`t take a BYTELENGTH, we take
                          NUMBER OF CALLS to store!

  IF you e.g. have an callerslog on NODE1 with a length of 400.000bytes and
   it stores about 200 calls ... What would you like to have? A callerslog
 which`s always around 100k or a callerslog where ALWAYS the last xx caller
                                   are in?

Guess this differs from person to person but some friends of mine and myself
                 are prefering a constant number of callers.





                         The commandline is SIMPLE!

        SAD-CLC.exe <calleslog> [outfile=<destinationfile>] <amount>

       Where callerslog is the PATH and NAME to your callerslog file1

                         e.g.: BBS:node1/Callerslog

    Wehere OUTFILE=xxx is the Destination callerslog file. This option is
    not needed! If you leave it out the old callerslog will be cloned and
    get get an extension ".old" and the stripped version will be directly
                       written over the original file.

       Where AMOUNT is the number of calls to store in the callersog.

                     A full line may shpw the following

        SAD-CLC.exe bbs:node1/callerslog outfile=ram:newcallerslog 50

       This will make a callerslog of 50 entrys at "ram:newcallerslog"

  If the old callerslog has less than 50 entrys CLC will interrupt the work
                           and won`t do anything!





